874,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":10.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.857802382148383,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.011485223752629628,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":29.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":1.5582437567923093,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.004832201926199486,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":54.8,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0046577224020018845,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":4.7,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07954681021565221,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":99.5,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.20855319585377402,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.014780001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Pinterest, Inc. operates as a visual search and discovery platform in the United States, Canada, Europe, and internationally. The company's platform allows people to find ideas, such as recipes, home and style inspiration, and others; and to search, save, and shop the ideas. It also provides various advertising products to help advertisers meet users; and ad auction that allows to serve ads to users at relevant moments while optimizing business outcomes for advertisers. The company was formerly known as Cold Brew Labs Inc. and changed its name to Pinterest, Inc. in April 2012. Pinterest, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William J. Ready | CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $813K ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $241K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $170K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Pinterest, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $11.7B market cap on $4.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +21.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 21% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 65% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6535397072577688},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Communication Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Pinterest (PINS) Could Be 21% Undervalued After Control Payout Changes","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-pins/pinterest/news/pinterest-pins-could-be-21-undervalued-after-control-payout","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795785076.186,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.4